{
  "name": "Classify failed Stripe payments by decline code",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Classify failed Stripe payments by decline code\n\n**Who it's for:** anyone billing subscriptions on Stripe who wants to react to a failed payment the right way instead of retrying blindly.\n\n### How it works\n1. Stripe sends an `invoice.payment_failed` event to the webhook.\n2. Duplicate events are dropped (Stripe re-sends webhooks).\n3. The workflow fetches the payment intent, because the real decline code lives there, not on the invoice.\n4. The code is classified into one of four recovery plans: hard decline (never retry, ask for a new card), insufficient funds (retry near payday), technical error (retry within hours), or soft decline (standard retries).\n5. It also reports whether Stripe itself will retry: if `next_payment_attempt` is empty, Stripe has given up on that invoice.\n6. A Switch sends each case down its own branch, ready for your email, Slack, or retry logic.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your Stripe credential to **Get payment intent from Stripe**.\n2. Activate the workflow and copy the webhook's Production URL.\n3. In Stripe: Developers, Webhooks, add an endpoint with that URL and the event `invoice.payment_failed`.\n4. Test with a Stripe test-mode card that declines.\n\n### Customization tips\nEdit the code lists in **Set decline code groups** to move a decline code to another plan. Replace the four placeholder nodes at the end with your own actions.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 860
      },
      "id": "s0",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Receive and dedupe\nStripe's event arrives and repeats are dropped.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 320,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "s1",
      "name": "Section: receive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Read the real decline code\nYour code groups, the payment intent from Stripe, then the classification.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 320,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "s2",
      "name": "Section: decline code",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        500,
        280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Route by recovery plan\nOne branch per plan. Replace the placeholders with your own actions.",
        "width": 620,
        "height": 760,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "s3",
      "name": "Section: route",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1300,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "stripe-failed-payment",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "n1",
      "name": "Receive Stripe failed payment event",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Stripe re-sends webhooks. Drop any event id we have already seen (keeps the last 500).\nconst e = $input.first().json.body ?? $input.first().json;\nconst s = $getWorkflowStaticData(\"global\");\ns.seen = s.seen || [];\nif (e.id && s.seen.includes(e.id)) { return []; }\nif (e.id) { s.seen.push(e.id); if (s.seen.length > 500) s.seen = s.seen.slice(-500); }\nreturn $input.all();"
      },
      "id": "n2",
      "name": "Skip duplicate events",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "hardDeclineCodes",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "expired_card, incorrect_number, invalid_number, lost_card, stolen_card, pickup_card, invalid_account, account_closed, no_such_card"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "insufficientFundsCodes",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "insufficient_funds"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "technicalErrorCodes",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "processing_error, issuer_not_available, try_again_later, reenter_transaction"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "n3",
      "name": "Set decline code groups",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        560,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "=https://api.stripe.com/v1/payment_intents/{{ ($json.body?.data?.object?.payment_intent || '').toString().replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_]/g, '') }}",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "stripeApi",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "n4",
      "name": "Get payment intent from Stripe",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        800,
        420
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Read the REAL decline code from the payment intent and pick a recovery plan.\nconst pi = $input.first().json || {};\nconst cfg = $(\"Set decline code groups\").first().json;\nconst w = $(\"Receive Stripe failed payment event\").first().json;\nconst evt = w.body ? w.body : w;\nconst o = (evt.data && evt.data.object) ? evt.data.object : {};\nconst list = (v) => String(v || \"\").split(\",\").map(x => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);\nconst lpe = pi.last_payment_error || null;\nconst code = lpe ? (lpe.decline_code || lpe.code) : \"unknown\";\nlet route = \"soft_retry\", action = \"Retry in 1, 3 and 7 days, then email the customer.\";\nif (list(cfg.hardDeclineCodes).includes(code)) { route = \"hard_no_retry\"; action = \"Do not retry. Email the customer a card-update link now.\"; }\nelse if (list(cfg.insufficientFundsCodes).includes(code)) { route = \"payday_retry\"; action = \"Retry after 24 hours, then on the 1st or 15th (payday).\"; }\nelse if (list(cfg.technicalErrorCodes).includes(code)) { route = \"technical_retry\"; action = \"Retry in 1, 6 and 24 hours. These usually clear on their own.\"; }\n// next_payment_attempt empty on the event = Stripe itself will NOT retry this invoice again.\nconst stripeWillRetry = (\"next_payment_attempt\" in o) ? !!o.next_payment_attempt : null;\nreturn [{ json: { invoice: o.id, customer: o.customer, email: o.customer_email || \"\", amount: (o.amount_due || 0) / 100, currency: o.currency || \"usd\",\n  declineCode: code, route, action, stripeWillRetry, attempt: o.attempt_count || 1 } }];"
      },
      "id": "n5",
      "name": "Classify decline and suggest action",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1040,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "strict",
                  "version": 2
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "c-hard_no_retry",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.route }}",
                    "rightValue": "hard_no_retry",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Hard decline"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "strict",
                  "version": 2
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "c-payday_retry",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.route }}",
                    "rightValue": "payday_retry",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Insufficient funds"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "strict",
                  "version": 2
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "c-technical_retry",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.route }}",
                    "rightValue": "technical_retry",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Technical error"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": true,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "strict",
                  "version": 2
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "c-soft_retry",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.route }}",
                    "rightValue": "soft_retry",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "equals"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "Soft decline"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "n6",
      "name": "Route by recovery plan",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "typeVersion": 3.2,
      "position": [
        1360,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "n7",
      "name": "Hard decline: ask for a new card",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "n8",
      "name": "Insufficient funds: retry near payday",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        340
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "n9",
      "name": "Technical error: retry within hours",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        500
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "n10",
      "name": "Soft decline: standard retries",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        660
      ]
    }
  ],
